lesson g6-puzzles-on-the-moon v=1 format=puzzles grade=6 unit=9 subject=maths levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Puzzles on the moon"
  goal "Solve problems with no method to follow, by drawing, listing or trying and checking, and prove the answer."

  puzzle stars=1 {
    show puzzle.moon-wall a=-4 b=4 c=6 easy-a=8 easy-b=2 easy-c=-3 hard-a=-7 hard-b=-6 hard-c=-5
  }
  puzzle stars=1 {
    show puzzle.base-walkway v=2 easy-v=0 hard-v=5
  }
  puzzle stars=2 {
    show puzzle.three-sisters-base y=27 a=3 b=4 easy-y=24 easy-a=2 easy-b=2 hard-y=30 hard-a=5 hard-b=4
  }
  puzzle stars=2 {
    show puzzle.crew-third-left v=2 easy-v=0 hard-v=5
  }
  puzzle stars=2 {
    show puzzle.oxygen-leak v=2 easy-v=0 hard-v=5
  }
  puzzle stars=3 {
    show puzzle.fewest-filters e=4 easy-e=0 hard-e=3
  }
  puzzle stars=3 {
    show puzzle.base-handshakes n=7 easy-n=5 hard-n=9
  }
  puzzle stars=3 {
    show puzzle.crater-routes m=2 n=4 easy-m=2 easy-n=3 hard-m=3 hard-n=4
  }
  puzzle stars=3 {
    show puzzle.panel-squares m=3 n=4 easy-m=2 easy-n=4 hard-m=4 hard-n=5
  }
  puzzle stars=3 {
    show puzzle.crater-lap v=3 easy-v=1 hard-v=5
  }

  grown-ups """
    These are meant to take time, and a puzzle put down on Tuesday and finished on Saturday has
    taught more than one finished by being told. Every one can be started by drawing or trying. The
    walkway adds its speed to Kai's or takes it away, and the rovers on the rim are a line with two
    dots on it, the gap growing by the difference of the speeds each hour until it is a whole rim.
    The sisters are three bars, and taking the extra lengths away leaves three equal ones. The crew
    and the tank are fractions of one whole: what went out leaves a fraction behind, and the pump's
    fraction an hour take away the crack's is what the tank gains. For the filters, picture the
    unluckiest order they could come out in. The handshakes, routes and squares all yield to a small
    case first and a table that grows one step at a time. A child who gets stuck here has not failed
    the lesson.
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the number wall has one number below zero on the bottom row, Kai walks at 2 m a second with a walkway of 1 m a second, the sisters are two years apart each, half and a third of the crew go out, the pump takes 2 hours against a 3-hour leak, the filters asked for are two of a colour, there are 10 handshakes, the grid is 2 by 3, the panel field is 2 by 4, and the rim is 12 km with speeds of 4 and 6."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level every number on the bottom of the wall is below zero, Kai walks against a walkway of 2 m a second at 5 m a second, the sisters are 4 and 5 years apart, a quarter and a fifth of the crew go out, the pump takes 6 hours against a 10-hour leak, the filters asked for are three red ones, there are 36 handshakes, the grid is 3 by 4, the panel field is 4 by 5, and the rim is 16 km with speeds of 5 and 9."
  }
}
